laws "Python Backend Laws" version 1

law tenant-isolation
  says "Never read or export another tenant's customer records."
  why  "Strict tenant isolation prevents cross-customer data leaks."
  on   action read of CustomerRecord
  forbid when resource.tenant_id != principal.tenant_id
  permit when resource.tenant_id == principal.tenant_id
  evidence tested by command "pytest tests/test_tenant_isolation.py"

law export-needs-approval
  says "Sending customer data outside the service requires human approval."
  why  "External exports are not reversible."
  on   action export of CustomerRecord
  ask  when context.destination.external
  evidence watched

law auth-covered-by-pytest
  says "Authentication and permission code is covered by automated pytest checks."
  why  "Every auth edit must pass deterministic regression checks."
  on   code "app/auth/**", "app/permissions/**"
  evidence tested by command "pytest tests/test_auth.py"
